text:
**C1: confirmed.** `findUser` returns `User | undefined` (`src/users.ts:17-18`), and `removeUser` only deletes the entry from the map (`src/users.ts:13-14`). `placeOrder` never checks that the user exists, and the user's orders stay in the array after removal (`src/orders.ts:9-10`). So `receiptHeader` can easily get an order whose user is missing. The `!` only quiets the type checker, and then `user.name` throws a TypeError (`src/receipts.ts:5-6`). This crash can happen in normal use, so I rate it blocking.

**C2: confirmed, but minor.** No test covers `receiptHeader`. In fact the repository has no tests or test setup at all: the only files are `src/orders.ts`, `src/receipts.ts`, `src/users.ts` and `REVIEW.md`. None of the repository's rules asks for tests. Adding one is a reasonable suggestion, not something that should hold up the merge.

